-- Shared pgTAP fixture: two companies with every company-owned table populated for both.
--
-- Included by test files with `\ir fixtures/two_companies.psql` AFTER their `begin;`, so every row is
-- created inside the test's transaction and removed by its `rollback;`. The database itself holds no
-- data. Runs as the database owner (postgres), like the backend's service role, so the
-- signed-in-user guards do not apply to the setup.
--
-- Companies: Nexus Solution (initials NS) and Kgalagadi Property Holdings (KP).
-- Users (all active, password-less; tests impersonate them with request.jwt.claims):
--   thandi.mokoena@nexussolution.co.za   NS company_admin
--   sipho.dlamini@nexussolution.co.za    NS property_manager and KP property_manager
--   naledi.vdmerwe@nexussolution.co.za   NS property_manager
--   kabelo.molefe@nexussolution.co.za    NS read_only
--   pieter@bothafamilytrust.co.za        NS property_owner
--   zanele.khumalo@khumaloinvest.co.za   NS property_owner
--   lerato@kgalagadiproperty.co.za       KP property_owner
-- Notable rows: NS leases WIP-L003 and DVC-L003 are unverified; NS has exactly one pending_review
-- statement extraction (on a review_required statement); each company has exactly one tenant message
-- awaiting approval (status pending_approval with a pending approval request).

\set QUIET on

